<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- What Android draws between the tap and the engine's first frame.

     The colour and nothing else, deliberately.

     It used to centre `rotelyx_splash.png` on it. That made three things happen
     in a row on every cold start: the system's own splash with the application
     icon, then this static mark, and then the mark assembling itself in Flutter.
     The same logo three times, the first two of them still.

     So this is now the ground the assembly happens on, and the handover from
     the system to Flutter is one unbroken colour. The colour is Tone.dBackdrop
     from lib/ui/theme.dart. The system half is in values-v31/styles.xml, which
     is where Android 12 and later moved that decision. -->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item android:drawable="@color/rotelyx_backdrop" />
</layer-list>
